                <pb facs="0054" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v15/pg21"/>

                <head>7. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On July 8, 1972, at Washington, Secretary of Commerce Peter G. Peterson, U.S. Chairman of the
                    U.S.-Soviet Joint Commercial Commission; Secretary of Agriculture Earl L. Butz;
                    and M.R. Kuzmin, First Deputy Minister of Foreign Trade of the USSR, signed an agreement regarding Soviet grain
                    purchases in the United States. The three-year agreement provided for Soviet
                    purchases of a total of $750 million in U.S. grains, the largest Soviet purchase
                    of U.S. grain to date. (Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin,</hi> July 31, 1972, pages 144–145)</p>
            </div>
